<p class="caption">
  No mean is headlined anywhere on this page. The distributions are skewed by
  per-invocation fixed costs and by a small number of very long tails — the
  slowest single invocation in this freeze is{' '}
  {formatMs(Math.max(...model.adapters.map((a) => a.whole.max)))}, against a
  page-wide fastest median of {formatMs(fastest.whole.median)} — and a mean
  over that shape would describe neither the typical case nor the tail.
  The adapters span roughly{' '}
  {Math.round(slowest.whole.median / fastest.whole.median)}× between the
  fastest and slowest medians, which is the order-of-magnitude claim this tier
  is entitled to make, and the strongest one it makes.
</p>

<h2 id="phases">Phase decomposition, within each adapter that has one</h2>

<p>
  Only the {decomposed.length} adapters whose declared row has phases appear
  here, and each is read <em>down its own column</em>. These numbers exist to
  decompose one adapter's own cost. Racing one adapter's phase against
  another's total is exactly the reading the granularity rule forbids. Each
  adapter's numbers open from its own disclosure, one per adapter, which is
  also the boundary the comparison rule draws.
</p>

{decomposed.map((adapter) => (
  <>
    <h3>
      <span
        class:list={['vendor-dot', vendorColorClass(adapter.tool)]}
        aria-hidden="true"></span>
      {vendorName(adapter.tool)} {toolVersionLabel(adapter.tool, adapter.toolVersion)}
    </h3>
    <details class="data-table">
      <summary>
        {`Show the data table — ${vendorName(adapter.tool)}'s ${
          adapter.phases.length
        } phases against its whole invocation`}
      </summary>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Phase</th>
              <th>Median</th>
              <th>Q1</th>
              <th>Q3</th>
              <th>Min</th>
              <th>Max</th>
              <th>Share of the median invocation</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {adapter.phases.map((phase) => (
              <tr>
                <td><code>{phase.phase}</code></td>
                <td><strong>{formatMs(phase.median)}</strong></td>
                <td>{formatMs(phase.q1)}</td>
                <td>{formatMs(phase.q3)}</td>
                <td>{formatMs(phase.min)}</td>
                <td>{formatMs(phase.max)}</td>
                <td class="muted">
                  {`${Math.round((phase.median / adapter.whole.median) * 100)}%`}
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))}
            <tr>
              <td><strong>whole invocation</strong></td>
              <td><strong>{formatMs(adapter.whole.median)}</strong></td>
              <td>{formatMs(adapter.whole.q1)}</td>
              <td>{formatMs(adapter.whole.q3)}</td>
              <td>{formatMs(adapter.whole.min)}</td>
              <td>{formatMs(adapter.whole.max)}</td>
