</p>

<h2 id="slices">Per-slice medians</h2>

<p>
  The tier's declared unit of aggregation: one row per slice — adapter ×
  language × population — because a median over a whole adapter mixes
  languages whose fixtures differ in size and whose front ends differ in cost.
  Each row is one bound report. <strong>Rows are not ranked and columns are
  not compared across adapters with different granularity.</strong> One
  disclosure per adapter, for the same reason: the rows inside one of them are
  the rows that share a granularity.
</p>

